# --- JumpReLUMatryoshka (agent0, EXP-001 hypothesis) ---
# Every architecture above (135+ prior experiments plus this campaign) builds on
# BatchTopK: a single global scalar cutoff shared by all 4096 features, forcing
# exactly k active features per batch regardless of how many ground-truth
# features actually fired. JumpReLU is a genuinely different sparsity family:
# each feature learns its OWN threshold via an L0 penalty (no hard top-k), so
# rare/high-magnitude features and common/low-magnitude features each find a
# natural cutoff instead of competing for a fixed slot budget. This should
# better match SynthSAEBench's per-sample F1 when the true active-feature count
# varies, which a fixed-k scheme cannot represent no matter how it's tuned.
# We keep the two things proven to help in this campaign (freq-sorted Matryoshka
# nesting, detached inner decode) and swap only the sparsity mechanism.

